# Lombok — TokenRealty

Human doc: [docs/rules/lombok.md](../../docs/rules/lombok.md).

Lombok is declared per service `pom.xml` (`provided` scope). Use it to remove boilerplate — not to hide business invariants.

## Use

| Annotation | Where |
|------------|--------|
| `@RequiredArgsConstructor` | `@Service`, `@Component`, `@RestController` with `final` dependencies |
| `@Getter` / `@Setter` | JPA entities in `entity/` or `adapter/out/persistence/` |
| `@NoArgsConstructor(access = PROTECTED)` | JPA entities (Hibernate requirement) |
| `@AllArgsConstructor` | JPA entities, simple value holders |
| `@Builder` | JPA entities, outbox rows, test fixtures |
| `@Slf4j` | Services, publishers, exception handlers |

## Prefer Java records for

- HTTP request/response DTOs (`dto/*Dtos.java`)
- Kafka event payload records (`kafka/events/`)
- RestClient request/response types
- Commands and port result types

`@Builder` on records is **optional** — allowed for test/seed ergonomics (see `AuthDtos`, `MarketplaceDtos`).

## Do NOT use Lombok on

- Future rich domain models in `domain/` — no `@Data` / `@Setter` on aggregates
- `tokenrealty-security` shared library — keep plain Java
- Classes where `@ToString` / `@EqualsAndHashCode` would leak secrets (password hashes, private keys, full KYC payloads)

## JPA entity pattern

```java
@Entity
@Getter
@Setter
@NoArgsConstructor(access = AccessLevel.PROTECTED)
@AllArgsConstructor
@Builder
public class Payment extends BaseEntity { /* ... */ }
```

## Injection pattern

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class PaymentService {
    private final PaymentRepository paymentRepository;
}
```

Keep manual constructors when building `RestClient` in the constructor body.

## Forbidden

```java
@Data on JPA entities or domain aggregates
@SneakyThrows in production code
@Setter on future domain model classes
```
